8	// mask — one dispatch, one workgroup per token, for llama.cpp's MUL_MAT f32 +
9	// RELU + SUM_ROWS + the adds and the mask around them.
10	//
11	// The scorer is not attention and the difference is the rectifier. Each of the
12	// four heads dots its 128-wide query against a block's pooled key and the
13	// **positive** parts are summed: a head that disagrees contributes nothing
14	// rather than cancelling a head that agrees, which is DeepSeek's lightning
15	// indexer and is why there is no softmax anywhere in here.
16	//
17	// **Both operands are F32 tensors and the reference still evaluates this in
18	// fp16** (research/l2e-attention.md): computing it in f32 gives 3.52e-03 rms
19	// against llama.cpp, computing it in *float64* gives the same 3.52e-03 — so it
20	// is not precision on our side — and rounding both operands to halves gives
21	// 5.11e-05. The backend is putting an f32 matmul on the fp16 matrix cores. Our
22	// operands arrive as halves from llm_attn_idx.comp, so this kernel is that
23	// arithmetic rather than a model of it, and the fp16 the whole vertical
24	// computes in concedes nothing the reference keeps.
25	//
26	// The bias is the part that cannot be inferred from the graph.
27	//
28	//	a block past the last whole one      -inf, it does not exist
29	//	a block at or after this token's
30	//	  incomplete tail                    1e9, "always visible"
31	//	the spare block that collects every
32	//	  unpooled cell                      1e9
33	//	anything else                        0
34	//
