36	// cell SEQ_PAST + t, the cache holds SEQ_PAST + T of them, and the causal
37	// mask compares a cell against this token's *position*. On a fresh sequence
38	// SEQ_PAST is zero and every line below is what it was.
39	//
40	// 1e9 and not an infinity, so that it can never meet the mask's -inf and make
41	// a NaN. And the expansion to cells routes every cell past the last whole
42	// block to that one spare block, which is what makes the incomplete tail
43	// visible without giving it a score.
44	//
45	// What this kernel does **not** do is the selection. `top_k + ratio - 1` is
46	// 2051 against a 256-cell cache, so it names every cell and is bit-identical
47	// to not selecting at all — and llama.cpp's own TOP_K turns out to be a
